{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHotkeySequenceRecorder"},{"type":"text","value":" to record an ordered sequence of chords. Recording defaults to physical codes, such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"['[KeyG]', 'Alt+[KeyS]']"},{"type":"text","value":". Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recordBy: 'key'"},{"type":"text","value":" for logical characters. Pass the saved array directly to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHotkeySequence"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Hotkeys automatically suppresses registered hotkey and sequence callbacks while any recorder is active. You do not need to set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enabled"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isRecording"},{"type":"text","value":". Registrations remain available for conflict detection, and recorded keys stay suppressed through repeats and key release."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"reactive-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reactive options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recorder options support "},{"type":"link","href":"./hotkeys.md#property-getters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"property getters and functions returning options"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Updated callbacks, validation, and recording settings apply during an active session without restarting it."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"basic-usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic usage"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import Component from '@glimmer/component'\nimport { tracked } from '@glimmer/tracking'\nimport { on } from '@ember/modifier'\nimport { useHotkeySequence, useHotkeySequenceRecorder, formatForDisplay } from '@tanstack/ember-hotkeys'\nimport type { HotkeySequence } from '@tanstack/ember-hotkeys'\n\nexport default class SequenceSettings extends Component {\n\t@tracked binding: HotkeySequence = ['G', 'G']\n\trecorder = useHotkeySequenceRecorder(this, {\n\t\tonRecord: (sequence) => { this.binding = sequence },\n\t})\n\tgoToTop = () => console.log('Go to top')\n\tget preview() { return this.recorder.steps.map((step) => formatForDisplay(step)).join(' → ') }\n\n\t<template>\n\t\t{{useHotkeySequence this.binding this.goToTop}}\n\t\t<button type=\"button\" {{on 'click' this.recorder.startRecording}}>Record sequence</button>\n\t\t{{#if this.recorder.isRecording}}\n\t\t\t<p>{{this.preview}}</p>\n\t\t\t<button type=\"button\" {{on 'click' this.recorder.commitRecording}}>Save</button>\n\t\t\t<button type=\"button\" {{on 'click' this.recorder.cancelRecording}}>Cancel</button>\n\t\t{{/if}}\n\t</template>\n}","lang":"gts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Press and release each chord, then press Enter or click Save. Cancellation leaves the saved binding unchanged."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"return-value","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return value"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Property"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isRecording"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whether a session is active."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"steps"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeySequence"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chords captured in the current session."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recordedSequence"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeySequence | null"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The last committed sequence."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"startRecording"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Start a new session."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stopRecording"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stop without calling "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onRecord"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onCancel"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cancelRecording"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Discard the session and call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onCancel"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"commitRecording"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Commit current steps; do nothing if empty."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read state through the recorder object. Destructuring its reactive getters once captures a snapshot."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recordBy"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'code'"},{"type":"text","value":" by default, or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'key'"},{"type":"text","value":" for logical characters. Missing physical codes never fall back to logical recording."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onRecord(sequence)"},{"type":"text","value":": called when a nonempty sequence is committed. Clearing calls only "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onClear"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onCancel"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onClear"},{"type":"text","value":": handle cancellation and removal of a saved binding."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"commitKeys"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'enter'"},{"type":"text","value":" by default. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'none'"},{"type":"text","value":" for manual or idle-timeout commit; plain Enter can then be recorded as a chord."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"commitOnEnter"},{"type":"text","value":": with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"commitKeys: 'enter'"},{"type":"text","value":", set this to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" to record Enter as a chord and finish another way."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"idleTimeoutMs"},{"type":"text","value":": commit after this many milliseconds of inactivity following a completed chord. No timer runs while waiting for the first chord."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"platform"},{"type":"text","value":": override platform detection for portable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Mod"},{"type":"text","value":" conversion."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"shared-defaults","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shared defaults"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createHotkeysScope"},{"type":"text","value":". The scope accepts "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hotkey"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hotkeySequence"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hotkeyRecorder"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hotkeySequenceRecorder"},{"type":"text","value":" options. Use the returned contextual helpers and recorder factories. Pass the scope through component arguments to share it with descendants; helpers and recorders still clean up with their own owners. Pass a getter for tracked defaults. Call-specific options override scope defaults, and per-definition options override common options. Omitted options use the core defaults. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../quick-start.md#shared-defaults","children":[{"type":"text","value":"shared defaults"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for a complete example. Options getters are read during recording and commit, so policy and callback changes also apply to active sessions."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"ignoreinputs","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ignoreInputs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", so normal typing in inputs, textareas, selects, and contentEditable elements passes through. Escape still cancels. Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ignoreInputs: false"},{"type":"text","value":" to record in a focused input."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"validation-and-conflicts","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validation and conflicts"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"validate(sequence, { events, parsedSequence })"},{"type":"text","value":" runs when committing and returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":", or a rejection message. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"detectConflicts"},{"type":"text","value":" checks single bindings and sequence prefixes. A rejected commit keeps the session active and the steps intact, so the user can edit them with Backspace."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The recorder supports the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"detectConflicts"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"validate"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onReject"},{"type":"text","value":" options as the "},{"type":"link","href":"./hotkey-recording.md#validation-and-conflicts","children":[{"type":"text","value":"single-hotkey recorder"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Use live registration IDs to exclude the binding being edited. Physical/logical overlap is based on the captured events, not a guessed keyboard layout."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"behavior","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Behavior"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Input"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Behavior"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Valid chord"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Append to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"steps"},{"type":"text","value":" and continue listening."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unmodified Enter with default commit settings and nonempty steps"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Commit and call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onRecord"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Escape"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cancel and call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onCancel"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unmodified Backspace or Delete with nonempty steps"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Remove the last step without committing."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unmodified Backspace or Delete with empty steps"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stop and call only "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onClear"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Modifier-only press, repeat, or IME composition"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do not append a step."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recorded chords use portable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Mod"},{"type":"text","value":". Recording events, commit keys, and their releases are isolated from application hotkeys and sequences. Code mode rejects AltGraph character entry; key mode preserves the produced character without synthetic Control/Alt."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"under-the-hood","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Under the hood"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ember owns the core Store subscription and recorder through the supplied owner. Destruction cancels active recording and releases listeners."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../examples/useHotkeySequenceRecorder","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useHotkeySequenceRecorder example"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for editable sequence settings and the "},{"type":"link","href":"../examples/kitchen-sink","children":[{"type":"text","value":"kitchen sink"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for manual commit, idle timeout, validation, and conflict feedback."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"reactive-options","text":"Reactive options","level":2},{"id":"basic-usage","text":"Basic usage","level":2},{"id":"return-value","text":"Return value","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":2},{"id":"shared-defaults","text":"Shared defaults","level":3},{"id":"ignoreinputs","text":"ignoreInputs","level":3},{"id":"validation-and-conflicts","text":"Validation and conflicts","level":2},{"id":"behavior","text":"Behavior","level":2},{"id":"under-the-hood","text":"Under the hood","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nUse `useHotkeySequenceRecorder` to record an ordered sequence of chords. Recording defaults to physical codes, such as `['[KeyG]', 'Alt+[KeyS]']`. Use `recordBy: 'key'` for logical characters. Pass the saved array directly to `useHotkeySequence`.\n\nTanStack Hotkeys automatically suppresses registered hotkey and sequence callbacks while any recorder is active. You do not need to set `enabled` from `isRecording`. Registrations remain available for conflict detection, and recorded keys stay suppressed through repeats and key release.\n\n## Reactive options\n\nRecorder options support [property getters and functions returning options](./hotkeys.md#property-getters). Updated callbacks, validation, and recording settings apply during an active session without restarting it.\n\n## Basic usage\n\n\n```gts\nimport Component from '@glimmer/component'\nimport { tracked } from '@glimmer/tracking'\nimport { on } from '@ember/modifier'\nimport { useHotkeySequence, useHotkeySequenceRecorder, formatForDisplay } from '@tanstack/ember-hotkeys'\nimport type { HotkeySequence } from '@tanstack/ember-hotkeys'\n\nexport default class SequenceSettings extends Component {\n\t@tracked binding: HotkeySequence = ['G', 'G']\n\trecorder = useHotkeySequenceRecorder(this, {\n\t\tonRecord: (sequence) => { this.binding = sequence },\n\t})\n\tgoToTop = () => console.log('Go to top')\n\tget preview() { return this.recorder.steps.map((step) => formatForDisplay(step)).join(' → ') }\n\n\t<template>\n\t\t{{useHotkeySequence this.binding this.goToTop}}\n\t\t<button type=\"button\" {{on 'click' this.recorder.startRecording}}>Record sequence</button>\n\t\t{{#if this.recorder.isRecording}}\n\t\t\t<p>{{this.preview}}</p>\n\t\t\t<button type=\"button\" {{on 'click' this.recorder.commitRecording}}>Save</button>\n\t\t\t<button type=\"button\" {{on 'click' this.recorder.cancelRecording}}>Cancel</button>\n\t\t{{/if}}\n\t</template>\n}\n```\n\nPress and release each chord, then press Enter or click Save. Cancellation leaves the saved binding unchanged.\n\n## Return value\n\n| Property | Type | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `isRecording` | `boolean` | Whether a session is active. |\n| `steps` | `HotkeySequence` | Chords captured in the current session. |\n| `recordedSequence` | `HotkeySequence \\| null` | The last committed sequence. |\n| `startRecording` | `() => void` | Start a new session. |\n| `stopRecording` | `() => void` | Stop without calling `onRecord` or `onCancel`. |\n| `cancelRecording` | `() => void` | Discard the session and call `onCancel`. |\n| `commitRecording` | `() => void` | Commit current steps; do nothing if empty. |\n\nRead state through the recorder object. Destructuring its reactive getters once captures a snapshot.\n\n## Options\n\n- `recordBy`: `'code'` by default, or `'key'` for logical characters. Missing physical codes never fall back to logical recording.\n- `onRecord(sequence)`: called when a nonempty sequence is committed. Clearing calls only `onClear`.\n- `onCancel` and `onClear`: handle cancellation and removal of a saved binding.\n- `commitKeys`: `'enter'` by default. Use `'none'` for manual or idle-timeout commit; plain Enter can then be recorded as a chord.\n- `commitOnEnter`: with `commitKeys: 'enter'`, set this to `false` to record Enter as a chord and finish another way.\n- `idleTimeoutMs`: commit after this many milliseconds of inactivity following a completed chord. No timer runs while waiting for the first chord.\n- `platform`: override platform detection for portable `Mod` conversion.\n\n### Shared defaults\n\nPass defaults to `createHotkeysScope`. The scope accepts `hotkey`, `hotkeySequence`, `hotkeyRecorder`, and `hotkeySequenceRecorder` options. Use the returned contextual helpers and recorder factories. Pass the scope through component arguments to share it with descendants; helpers and recorders still clean up with their own owners. Pass a getter for tracked defaults. Call-specific options override scope defaults, and per-definition options override common options. Omitted options use the core defaults. See [shared defaults](../quick-start.md#shared-defaults) for a complete example. Options getters are read during recording and commit, so policy and callback changes also apply to active sessions.\n\n### `ignoreInputs`\n\nThe default is `true`, so normal typing in inputs, textareas, selects, and contentEditable elements passes through. Escape still cancels. Set `ignoreInputs: false` to record in a focused input.\n\n## Validation and conflicts\n\n`validate(sequence, { events, parsedSequence })` runs when committing and returns `true`, `false`, or a rejection message. `detectConflicts` checks single bindings and sequence prefixes. A rejected commit keeps the session active and the steps intact, so the user can edit them with Backspace.\n\nThe recorder supports the same `detectConflicts`, `validate`, and `onReject` options as the [single-hotkey recorder](./hotkey-recording.md#validation-and-conflicts). Use live registration IDs to exclude the binding being edited. Physical/logical overlap is based on the captured events, not a guessed keyboard layout.\n\n## Behavior\n\n| Input | Behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| Valid chord | Append to `steps` and continue listening. |\n| Unmodified Enter with default commit settings and nonempty steps | Commit and call `onRecord`. |\n| Escape | Cancel and call `onCancel`. |\n| Unmodified Backspace or Delete with nonempty steps | Remove the last step without committing. |\n| Unmodified Backspace or Delete with empty steps | Stop and call only `onClear`. |\n| Modifier-only press, repeat, or IME composition | Do not append a step. |\n\nRecorded chords use portable `Mod`. Recording events, commit keys, and their releases are isolated from application hotkeys and sequences. Code mode rejects AltGraph character entry; key mode preserves the produced character without synthetic Control/Alt.\n\n## Under the hood\n\nEmber owns the core Store subscription and recorder through the supplied owner. Destruction cancels active recording and releases listeners.\n\nSee the [useHotkeySequenceRecorder example](../examples/useHotkeySequenceRecorder) for editable sequence settings and the [kitchen sink](../examples/kitchen-sink) for manual commit, idle timeout, validation, and conflict feedback.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Sequence Recording Guide\nid: sequence-recording\n---\n\nUse `useHotkeySequenceRecorder` to record an ordered sequence of chords. Recording defaults to physical codes, such as `['[KeyG]', 'Alt+[KeyS]']`. Use `recordBy: 'key'` for logical characters. Pass the saved array directly to `useHotkeySequence`.\n\nTanStack Hotkeys automatically suppresses registered hotkey and sequence callbacks while any recorder is active. You do not need to set `enabled` from `isRecording`. Registrations remain available for conflict detection, and recorded keys stay suppressed through repeats and key release.\n\n## Reactive options\n\nRecorder options support [property getters and functions returning options](./hotkeys.md#property-getters). Updated callbacks, validation, and recording settings apply during an active session without restarting it.\n\n## Basic usage\n\n\n```gts\nimport Component from '@glimmer/component'\nimport { tracked } from '@glimmer/tracking'\nimport { on } from '@ember/modifier'\nimport { useHotkeySequence, useHotkeySequenceRecorder, formatForDisplay } from '@tanstack/ember-hotkeys'\nimport type { HotkeySequence } from '@tanstack/ember-hotkeys'\n\nexport default class SequenceSettings extends Component {\n\t@tracked binding: HotkeySequence = ['G', 'G']\n\trecorder = useHotkeySequenceRecorder(this, {\n\t\tonRecord: (sequence) => { this.binding = sequence },\n\t})\n\tgoToTop = () => console.log('Go to top')\n\tget preview() { return this.recorder.steps.map((step) => formatForDisplay(step)).join(' → ') }\n\n\t<template>\n\t\t{{useHotkeySequence this.binding this.goToTop}}\n\t\t<button type=\"button\" {{on 'click' this.recorder.startRecording}}>Record sequence</button>\n\t\t{{#if this.recorder.isRecording}}\n\t\t\t<p>{{this.preview}}</p>\n\t\t\t<button type=\"button\" {{on 'click' this.recorder.commitRecording}}>Save</button>\n\t\t\t<button type=\"button\" {{on 'click' this.recorder.cancelRecording}}>Cancel</button>\n\t\t{{/if}}\n\t</template>\n}\n```\n\nPress and release each chord, then press Enter or click Save. Cancellation leaves the saved binding unchanged.\n\n## Return value\n\n| Property | Type | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `isRecording` | `boolean` | Whether a session is active. |\n| `steps` | `HotkeySequence` | Chords captured in the current session. |\n| `recordedSequence` | `HotkeySequence \\| null` | The last committed sequence. |\n| `startRecording` | `() => void` | Start a new session. |\n| `stopRecording` | `() => void` | Stop without calling `onRecord` or `onCancel`. |\n| `cancelRecording` | `() => void` | Discard the session and call `onCancel`. |\n| `commitRecording` | `() => void` | Commit current steps; do nothing if empty. |\n\nRead state through the recorder object. Destructuring its reactive getters once captures a snapshot.\n\n## Options\n\n- `recordBy`: `'code'` by default, or `'key'` for logical characters. Missing physical codes never fall back to logical recording.\n- `onRecord(sequence)`: called when a nonempty sequence is committed. Clearing calls only `onClear`.\n- `onCancel` and `onClear`: handle cancellation and removal of a saved binding.\n- `commitKeys`: `'enter'` by default. Use `'none'` for manual or idle-timeout commit; plain Enter can then be recorded as a chord.\n- `commitOnEnter`: with `commitKeys: 'enter'`, set this to `false` to record Enter as a chord and finish another way.\n- `idleTimeoutMs`: commit after this many milliseconds of inactivity following a completed chord. No timer runs while waiting for the first chord.\n- `platform`: override platform detection for portable `Mod` conversion.\n\n### Shared defaults\n\nPass defaults to `createHotkeysScope`. The scope accepts `hotkey`, `hotkeySequence`, `hotkeyRecorder`, and `hotkeySequenceRecorder` options. Use the returned contextual helpers and recorder factories. Pass the scope through component arguments to share it with descendants; helpers and recorders still clean up with their own owners. Pass a getter for tracked defaults. Call-specific options override scope defaults, and per-definition options override common options. Omitted options use the core defaults. See [shared defaults](../quick-start.md#shared-defaults) for a complete example. Options getters are read during recording and commit, so policy and callback changes also apply to active sessions.\n\n### `ignoreInputs`\n\nThe default is `true`, so normal typing in inputs, textareas, selects, and contentEditable elements passes through. Escape still cancels. Set `ignoreInputs: false` to record in a focused input.\n\n## Validation and conflicts\n\n`validate(sequence, { events, parsedSequence })` runs when committing and returns `true`, `false`, or a rejection message. `detectConflicts` checks single bindings and sequence prefixes. A rejected commit keeps the session active and the steps intact, so the user can edit them with Backspace.\n\nThe recorder supports the same `detectConflicts`, `validate`, and `onReject` options as the [single-hotkey recorder](./hotkey-recording.md#validation-and-conflicts). Use live registration IDs to exclude the binding being edited. Physical/logical overlap is based on the captured events, not a guessed keyboard layout.\n\n## Behavior\n\n| Input | Behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| Valid chord | Append to `steps` and continue listening. |\n| Unmodified Enter with default commit settings and nonempty steps | Commit and call `onRecord`. |\n| Escape | Cancel and call `onCancel`. |\n| Unmodified Backspace or Delete with nonempty steps | Remove the last step without committing. |\n| Unmodified Backspace or Delete with empty steps | Stop and call only `onClear`. |\n| Modifier-only press, repeat, or IME composition | Do not append a step. |\n\nRecorded chords use portable `Mod`. Recording events, commit keys, and their releases are isolated from application hotkeys and sequences. Code mode rejects AltGraph character entry; key mode preserves the produced character without synthetic Control/Alt.\n\n## Under the hood\n\nEmber owns the core Store subscription and recorder through the supplied owner. Destruction cancels active recording and releases listeners.\n\nSee the [useHotkeySequenceRecorder example](../examples/useHotkeySequenceRecorder) for editable sequence settings and the [kitchen sink](../examples/kitchen-sink) for manual commit, idle timeout, validation, and conflict feedback.\n"}
